entry=('The SAO v2 raw asset boundary reuses the source owner/unfinished-read promise and verifies exact index-bound JSON bytes plus scientific contract. Standard sealed static export now streams every adopted v2 tile through that owner with catalog/static accounting, while old envelope APIs remain API-only. Current client SAO tile reads use the same Sky encoded-file owner as images, under its unchanged combined byte/transfer budgets. JSON has independent byte identity, no raster dimensions; exact native UTF8 read bytes and every tile/source/scientific binding are checked. Native read cancellation rejects immediately but retains its file lease until the actual callback. Version2 inventory migrates known v1 image entries without orphan promotion; an invalid present v2 cannot revive a stale v1 pointer. Each delivered index has a small immutable publication/envelope wrapper with its originating file generation, sharing the full index; another observer refresh cannot reactivate a retired capability. No second parsed tile cache or expanded ordinary response-cache policy was added. Bounded current-at-execution HTTP pressure avoided the former 24-entry eviction and supplied static raw/warm/no-HTTP and late-native-read evidence; the final wrapper fix has a separate failing-before/consumer regression epoch. Actual page/Scene image+SAO integration must use one encoded owner across task modules. Old-binary rollback JSON inventory handling, full-app file/physical budgets, shared BFF loading, independent review and native/production capacity remain unverified. See [actual source epochs and remaining consumers](../../.codex/work-items/cloud-sky-native-2026-09-22/evidence/experience-sao-shared-files-and-static-2026-10-03.md).')
